these 76 afghan boys were caught by  turkish soldiers trying to cross the  border  from iran into turkey they had walked  for weeks  relying on smugglers to take them across  the rug mountain terrain  they were desperate to escape the  bombings and fighting in afghanistan  they now face being deported to iran but  they have no regrets and they say they'd  do it all again  if they had a chance of reaching  turkey's big cities  and then maybe onto europe for those who  manage to elude the turkish forces on  the border  and the police in the city it's time to  move on  they split up into smaller groups so as  not to draw attention to themselves  but all have a story to tell  i left college and came here if i stayed  i had to join the war  then my parents said i should leave the  country the taliban recruits young men  you get killed most of these young  afghans have been called by the  smugglers they paid to help them leave  afghanistan  and now they have no money left  we agreed on 750 with the smuggler and  already paid 500  the rest was to be paid when we reached  istanbul  but i had no more money so they left me  on the street  turkey has now ramped up security  measures at its border with iran  these migrants are stationed in  so-called safe houses  the police call them shock houses  waiting for the right moment  to continue their journey the smugglers  take money every day  if the afghans don't pay they get kicked  out there is no escape  doors are locked  i left afghanistan because of war and  misery the taliban are beating and  forcing my parents to cook royal food  for them  and here we are serve two meals a day by  the smuggler  there are about 35 people in this one  house including women and children  there is little air and no privacy  families are reluctant  to talk on camera  we came to turkey to work until the  borders get open then move to europe to  support our family  i worked in iran for six months and have  been here for 10 days  the smuggler says we need to wait here  until the security measures  ease with taliban it is not safe anymore  there is poverty and misery people  cannot pursue their normal lives anymore  in afghanistan  last year 61 asylum seekers on board a  fishing boat died after their boat  capsized in lake  van another 40 migrants have died this  year  this is the cemetery of the nameless the  migrants who wanted to escape bullets  and butchery in their own country  but who fell victim to human traffickers  despite obvious dangers fears are  growing in afghanistan  there will now be many more people who  are prepared to risk their  lives in the hope of finding something  better  elsewhere cinema al jazeera  von turkey
 

